    "chunk_text": "Extended proposals.\n\n10AIV ^w& fldgi \u2013 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h \u2013 2025'05'30\n\nP\u0d7a\u0d8b\u0d8d IV (A) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 30.05.2025\n\n(8) Notwithstanding anything contained in the above sections, a motion on a matter considered by a Committee of the Council and recommended for the decision of the Council shall be prepared in writing and submitted to the Secretary for inclusion in the agenda under the signature of the Chairman of the Committee or the member presiding over the Committee on that day.\n\n(9) Every motion included in the agenda shall be included in the same manner as the proposer made.\n\n(10) Every motion submitted for the agenda must be proposed to the House by the proposer himself or by another member with the permission of the proposer, in the manner speci\ufb01 ed in the agenda.\n\n(11) After any motion has been proposed to the Council, it shall be seconded by another member and until such motion has been seconded, no comment shall be made by the proposer or any other member on the motion.\n\n(12) Any member may second any motion or amendment to the motion after rising from his seat and saluting the Chairman, formally without prejudice to his right to speak on the motion at a later stage of the debate.\n\n(13) No motion shall be allowed to be submitted to the Council unless the Council is satis\ufb01 ed that it is necessary to present the motion to the Council on that day and that it would be in the public interest to take a decision on the motion at that day itself.\n\n(14) A motion submitted for the approval of the Council under sub-section (13) above shall be submitted to the Secretary with a written and signed statement by the proposer stating the reasons for the necessity of submitting the motion at the same session of the Council, together with a request to allow the motion to be presented at the meeting of the Council on that day."
