    "chunk_text": "(2) If the Council does not decide to approve the budget or supplementary budget as such under the \ufb01 rst sub-section above, the Council may decide to approve the relevant budget or supplementary budget with minor changes or rejections or with the addition to all or any subject of it.\n\nWithdrawing a proposal or amendment.\n\nResubmission a plan.\n\nCouncil approval regarding the budget.\n\nP\u0d7a\u0d8b\u0d8d IV (A) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 30.05.2025\n\n27. If any member made objection while the Chairman seeking the consent of the Council, at the end of the debate on any motion, the Chairman shall take a vote on the motion.\n\n28. (1) At every election in the Pradeshiya Sabha, the bell shall be rung in advance to invite the members present to participate in the voting and the voting shall be conducted two minutes after the bell is rung.\n\n(2) Unless the members present at a meeting of the Council avoid from voting, they shall cast their votes for or against.\n\n(3) The Secretary of the Council shall take and record the votes at the polls of the Council, and shall record the votes whether for, against or abstentions by name, starting from the Chairman,\n\n(4) The votes recorded by the Secretary shall be certi\ufb01 ed by him and announced to the Council.\n\n29. The Chairperson shall have an initial vote along with the other members, and in the event of an equality of votes for and against any motion or matter, the Chairperson shall have a casting vote.\n\n30. It shall be the duty of the Council to consider the reports of the Committees included and submitted with the agenda at the same time or to \ufb01 x a date for considering such reports.\n\nHowever, in the event of a review under this section, the provisions of sub-section (8) of this rule shall apply to the Council in deciding on any matter contained in such a report."
