    "chunk_size_bytes": 1320,
    "chunk_text": "1. Benedict XVI Catholic International Institute of Higher Education shall, when admitting students for the degree programme specified in Schedule II hereto in respect of the Bachelor of Science Honours in Counselling Psychology with a minimum of 120 Credits (SLQF Level 6), adhere to the minimum entry qualification of ;\n\n(a) Three (3) simple passes (S) in any stream in one and the same sitting at the G.C.E. (Advanced Level) Examination conducted by the Department of Examination of Sri Lanka or equivalent qualification; and\n\n(b) A simple pass (S) for General English at the G.C.E. (Advance Level) Examination conducted by the Department of Examination of Sri Lanka or equivalent qualification.\n\n2. Benedict XVI Catholic International Institute of Higher Education is recognized to offer the degree specified in Schedule II hereto subject to an initial review in 3 years from the date of recognition and the five (5) year periodic review conducted by the Specified Authority.\n\nSchedule II\n\nColumn IDegreeColumn IIAbbreviations for DegreeBachelor of Science Honours in Counselling PsychologyBSc Hons (Counselling Psychology)\n\nDr. Harini Amarasuriya, Minister of Education. Higher Education and Vocational Education.\n\nColombo,15th May, 2025.\n\nEOG 05 - 0200\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA."
